Inline atoms (phrasing-content tags: a, code, em, span, ...) never break open
under width pressure, and an all-inline children list no longer forces its
parent onto multiple lines. Author-multiline children still outrank atom
status (a `<code>` the author wrote multi-line renders multi-line, as a block
child), and the preserve tags (`textarea`, `script`) are never atoms regardless
of tag membership.

-- input.gsx --
package p

component GettingStarted() {
	<p class="text-muted-foreground">
		gsxui components are copy-in: the CLI vendors real <code>.gsx</code> source into your own
		module, so what you build against is code you own and can edit — not a package you import
		and can't touch.
	</p>
}

component OneLiner() {
	<p>vendors real <code>.gsx</code> source.</p>
}

component AuthorMultilineFallsBack() {
	<p>
		see
		<code>
			.gsx
		</code>
		file
	</p>
}

component NeverAtoms() {
	<textarea>hello world</textarea>
	<script>const x = 1;</script>
}
